Subject: [PATCH] Fritchii DownloadLanding: guest CPU writes wait for a buffer download landing under them, without the async read-back; fence downloads land per copy group (EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DOWNLOAD_LANDING, _STATS; off by default)

Port of Frizti/Fritchii 8f09b0fd90 (Frizti, branch oot-gather-fix; "core, video_core: let guest
writes wait for a download landing under them"), itself a port of zortos293/Lichii #805 4942eb8a39
(jpkto). On top of T85 (0001..0486); applies with 0487 (lichii-1094) and 0488 (lichii-1016) in
either order.

Why 7 of 10 hunks failed on T83: 0486 (Lichii #1028) brought the same protocol afterwards
(#1028's df0b5f6bde is #805's 4942eb8a39), but only inside EDEN_UP_L1028_ASYNC_READBACK. Hunk by
hunk, by intent (T85 line numbers):
- core/memory.cpp, DownloadLanding::Await after Collect: have (memory.cpp:927, :974, L1028 only,
  and only when Collect stored new bits). Here: also with this switch.
- rasterizer_download_area.h, the DownloadLanding class: have, same code (rasterizer_download_area.h:
  38-108). Here: a wait time for the stats.
- buffer_cache.h include, buffer_cache_base.h comment: have / updated.
- DownloadRangesMemory (landing, look after the wait): have (buffer_cache.h:572, L1028 only), but it
  looks with GuardedCpuWriteRanges (empty unless EDEN_NX2_DOWNLOAD_GUARDS >= 1, 0240). Here: with
  this switch too, and it looks at every collected write (CollectedCpuWriteRanges).
- DownloadMemoryRanges (2 hunks): we have no such function; its job (a read's download) is
  0486's read path (DownloadMemoryForRead/WriteReadDownloads), which always lands in a landing.
- PopAsyncBuffers (per copy, copies within a page together): partly; T85 lands a fence's downloads
  in one landing over their hull (buffer_cache.h:2337, L1028 only). Here: Fritchii's per group
  landings, each with its own look at every collected write, with this switch.
- DownloadBuffersMemory: have (buffer_cache.h:4639, L1028 only). Here: also with this switch,
  looking at every collected write.
- DownloadBufferMemory (look after the wait, mapped/staged/immediate): have as #1028 shaped it
  (begin_landing, buffer_cache.h:4695: the look before the wait is kept and the one after it is
  added). Here: also with this switch.
- Not in Fritchii, ours: FinishDownloadPieces (no staging buffer) lands like DownloadRangesMemory;
  GPU::GatherAndApply keeps gathered writes pending until applied (#1028's applying list,
  gpu.cpp:189/258, which Fritchii lacks: a fence download popped between a gather and its apply
  would not see those writes).
Other paths named in the task: EDEN_NX2_DMA_SNAPSHOT reads guest memory these landings write (no
change needed); 0471's copy barrier orders host transfers, not guest memory (no overlap); 0477
GRHAND's handed reads flush through DownloadMemory (covered); texture cache downloads
(PopAsyncFlushes, SwizzleImage) write guest memory under texture_cache.mutex with no look and are
NOT covered: DownloadLanding publishes one landing at a time and relies on buffer_cache.mutex for
that; EDEN_NX2_TC_KEEP_ASYNC concerns CPU texture decodes, not downloads.

What each switch does (Common::PeSwitch, exactly "1"; read once):
EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DOWNLOAD_LANDING=1: the protocol of L1028 without the async read-back: every buffer
  cache download writes guest memory inside a DownloadLanding after its host GPU wait and takes its
  look at the collected guest CPU writes inside it; a guest CPU write collected in a landing's
  range stores its bytes once the landing ended; gathered writes stay in the look until applied.
  A fence's downloads land per group of copies within a page of each other. Every look keeps every
  collected write, whatever EDEN_NX2_DOWNLOAD_GUARDS says, as Fritchii's always does (without the
  switch T85's looks find nothing at 0, play env v2.4's level; the hull path, taken only without
  it, is unchanged). The looks keep whole 64-byte blocks: GPU bytes sharing a block with a newer
  guest write are not written (guards >= 1 did the same; watch the "Download kept off newer CPU
  writes ... on command list pages" line, now also logged with this switch). Logs one line at the
  first use.
EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DOWNLOAD_LANDING_STATS=1 (no behaviour change; give it to control arms): every 10 s
  "Download landing (S s; landing on|off, L1028 on|off, guards G): landed F fence downloads (C copy
  group landings), Y synchronous, D read downloads, B KiB | late, kept off a newer guest CPU write:
  K downloads, K KiB skipped | late, lost, written over a guest CPU write collected before: L
  downloads, L KiB | late, raced, written under one collected since (upper bound): R downloads,
  R KiB | guest CPU writes held by a landing: N, T ms | early (lower bound): E area lookups of
  bytes whose fence download had not landed (KiB), W guest CPU writes over such bytes (KiB of
  fence downloads dropped)". Counts per window (not per second). Lost: the download's look did not
  keep a write already collected when it wrote (the guest's bytes were replaced by older GPU
  ones); 0 with the landing switch by construction (its looks keep them all), so compare the
  control's lost with the landing arm's kept off. Raced: written under a write collected after
  the look and still collected at the end (in a landing's range it waited; without one it is lost
  if stored first; writes made after the download wrote count too). Early lookups: only the first
  read into an area the core then keeps. Without either landing switch, writes gathered and not
  yet applied are invisible to the stats (GPU::ForEachPendingCpuWrite): lost and raced are lower
  bounds there.

Unset (both): T85 behaviour. What still runs: one static bool per Active()/StatsEnabled() test at
the sites L1028 already tests, the PopAsyncBuffers loop body moved into a lambda (same steps in the
same order; the hull landing, L1028 only, still lives to the end of the function), one static
bool test per WriteDownloadedMemory/ClaimCpuWrites/EndLandingStats/NoteLandingLook call and per
look (LandingCpuWriteRanges, LandingLookRanges). EDEN_UP_L1028_ASYNC_READBACK alone: T85 too.

Credit: Frizti (Fritchii 8f09b0fd90), jpkto (Lichii #805 4942eb8a39), zortos293 (Lichii #1028).

After review (first version sha256 9caf8499b8f72f6a): the looks of this switch keep every collected
write at any guard level (they found nothing at guards 0); the stats tell lost bytes from raced ones
and call the early reads area lookups, a lower bound; the unused MaybeReportIfEnabled was removed.

Checks (VM scratch, fritchii-download-landing_fix_checks.sh, log
fritchii-download-landing.fix-checks.log): git apply --check on T85 and a reverse dry run: OK. With
0487 (lichii-1094) and 0488 (lichii-1016) in either order, and with ubo-ahead.diff in either order:
line offsets only, same tree either way; the full stack 0487 + 0488 + this + ubo-ahead: no fuzz or
rejects. Shared files: buffer_cache.h and buffer_cache_base.h, no shared hunks. The derived gpu.cpp
and memory.cpp (headless/CMakeLists.txt) take the same change, their CMake anchors unchanged.
prepare-vulkan-port.py: 6 anchor skips before and after, the generated buffer_cache.h carries the
same change. -fsyntax-only with the build's flags: 51 TUs rc=0 (every TU that directly includes a
touched header, rasterizer_interface.h, gpu.h, fence_manager.h or renderer_base.h, from the tree,
the generated copies or the derived ones), and 11 TUs of the tree with ubo-ahead. Injected errors:
all 51 rc=1; the four buffer cache TUs reach all 20 buffer_cache.h markers. Host test of the patched
DownloadLanding (g++, 2 threads): a write under a landing waits for it, one elsewhere or after it
does not, WaitNs only with _STATS. Log format strings: 1/1 and 21/21 placeholders/arguments. Not
built, not run on the PS5.

